_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.12422051340855741,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.1338005484352633,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.28331015089975353,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.008003103998245508,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":42.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.08694537653041845,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.15368024030045363,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.02711,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":18.1,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Natera, Inc., a diagnostics company, engages in the development and commercialization of molecular testing services worldwide. It offers Signatera, a personalized ctDNA blood test for MRD assessment, early recurrence monitoring, and evaluation of treatment response in patients previously diagnosed with cancer; Latitude, a blood-based MRD test for colorectal cancer; Altera, a tissue based comprehensive genomic profiling test; and Empower, a hereditary cancer screening test. The company also provides Panorama, a non-invasive prenatal test; Horizon, a carrier screening test; Fetal Focus, a single-gene NIPT, or sgNIPT, that screens for 21 single-gene inherited conditions; and Vistara, a single-gene NIPT, which screens for 25 single-gene conditions. In addition, it offers Anora, which tests and analyzes miscarriage tissue from women who have experienced one or more pregnancy losses; Empower, a hereditary cancer screening test; Prospera, a test to assess active rejection in patients who have undergone solid organ transplantation; Renasight, a kidney gene panel test; and Constellation software, a cloud-based distribution model. Further, the company provides NateraCore, a platform to support the patient and provider experience; phlebotomy services; and EMR integration services. The company serves independent laboratories, national and regional reference laboratories, medical centers and physician practices for its screening tests, research laboratories, and pharmaceutical companies through its direct sales force and laboratory distribution partners, as well as Constellation licensees under its cloud-based distribution model. It has a partnership agreement with BGI Genomics Co., Ltd. to develop, manufacture, and commercialize NGS-based genetic testing assays for clinical and commercial use. The company was formerly known as Gene Security Network, LLC and changed its name to Natera, Inc. in January 2012. Natera, Inc. was founded in 2003 and is headquartered in Austin, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Steven Leonard Chapman | CEO & Director | Age 46 | Compensation: $2.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $376K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 28%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $18K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $58K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Natera, Inc. is a large-cap healthcare business with a $44.1B market cap on $2.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +41% over the past three years and +28% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -69% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $109M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -76.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 15% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 2.7% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 4017% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":40.1650106754378},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 13% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $28.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 1667% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (25.6% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Natera (NTRA) Faces A Valuation Gap, Is It Still Below Fair Value?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-ntra/natera/news/natera-ntra-faces-a-valuation-gap-is-it-still-below-fair-val","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795587003.873,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.863,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Natera (NASDAQ:NTRA) Facing A Turning Point In Healthcare Innovation?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/healthcare/is-natera-nasdaqntra-facing-a-turning-point-in-healthcare-innovation","date":"2026-11-23","timestamp":1795467420.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.452,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(NTRA) as a Liquidity Pulse for Institutional Tactics","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/150/NTRA_as_a_Liquidity_Pulse_for_Institutional_Tactics_112226052001_1795386001.html","date":"2026-11-22","timestamp":1795386001.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Natera, Inc. $NTRA Stock: Focus Advisor Solutions LLC Increases Holdings","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/natera-inc-ntra-stock-focus-advisor-solutions-llc-increases-holdings.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":